      "text": [
        " إِنَّ مِنْ أَشَدِّ النَّاسِ حَسْرَةً يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ مَنْ وَصَفَ عَدْلًا ثُمَّ عَمِلَ بِغَيْرِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Yusuf Al Bazzaz, from Moalla Bin Khunays, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one with the most intense of regrets on the Day of Judgment would be the one who portrayed the justice, then acted without it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Yusuf al- Bazzaz from Mu’alla ibn Khanis from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “One who, on the Day of Judgment, will regret the most is he who preaches justice but himself acts otherwise.” "
        ]
      }
    },
